    <div style=3D"text-align: center; font-weight: bold;">PURCHASE AND SALE=
 AGREEMENT</div>
    <div>&nbsp;</div>
    <div style=3D"text-align: justify;">This Purchase and Sale Agreement (=
=93Agreement=94) is made by and between <font style=3D"font-weight: bold;">=
Peck Electric Co., </font>a Vermont corporation with a place of business in=
 Williston, Vermont, as the =93<u>Seller</u>,
      and <font style=3D"font-weight: bold;">Nedde Real Estate LLC, </font>=
a Vermont limited liability company with a place of business in Burlington,=
 Vermont, as the =93<u>Buyer</u>=94, and is made and entered into as of the=
 date of execution by the last
      party to execute this Agreement (the =93<u>Effective Date</u>=94).</d=
iv>
    <div>&nbsp;</div>
    <div style=3D"text-align: center;"><u>Background</u></div>
    <div>&nbsp;</div>
    <div style=3D"text-align: justify;">Seller owns, in fee simple, the rea=
l property measuring =B12.28 acres known as and numbered 4090 Williston Rd.=
, South Burlington, Vermont (Parcel ID 1810-04090, SPAN 600-188-11381), whi=
ch is improved with a commercial
      building ( the =93<u>Building</u>=94), and Buyer wishes to purchase f=
rom Seller, and Seller wishes to sell to Buyer, all of Seller=92s right, ti=
tle and interest in and to such real property together with all improvement=
s thereon, including the Building but
      excluding the solar photovoltaic electricity generation facility inst=
alled on the rooftop of the Building (the =93<u>Solar</u><u>&nbsp;</u><u>Fa=
cility</u>=94), and together with all easements, permits, approvals, alloca=
tions and rights benefiting the same,
      which are collectively referred to herein as the =93<u>Property</u>=
=94.</div>
    <div><br>
    </div>
    <div style=3D"text-align: justify;">In consideration of the premises an=
d the mutual covenants and agreements herein set forth, and in reliance on =
the representations and warranties contained herein, Buyer and Seller hereb=
y agree as follows:</div>
    <div><br>
    </div>
    <div>Section 1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <font s=
tyle=3D"font-weight: bold;"><u>Sale and Purchase; Operation of Property</u>=
.</font></div>
    <div>&nbsp;</div>
    <div style=3D"text-align: justify; text-indent: 27pt;">(a)&nbsp;&nbsp;&=
nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Seller agrees to sell and convey the Proper=
ty to Buyer, and Buyer agrees to purchase the Property from Seller, subject=
 to the terms and conditions set forth herein. Included with the
      sale of the Property shall be (i) all of Seller=92 right, title and i=
nterest in and to all federal, state and local permits for the Property, (i=
i) all municipal allocations for the Property (including water supply and s=
ewer allocation), and (iii) all
      engineering plans, drawings, designs, site plans, surveys, and enviro=
nmental site assessments prepared for the Property.</div>
    <div style=3D"text-indent: 27pt;">&nbsp;</div>
    <div style=3D"text-align: justify; text-indent: 27pt;">(b)&nbsp;&nbsp;&=
nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; While this Agreement is in effect, Sell=
er shall not (i) enter into any leases or agreements with respect to the Pr=
operty and its operation, (ii) grant any easements or rights with respect
      to the Property or (iii) permit the attachment of any encumbrances to=
 the Property, in each instance without the prior written consent of Buyer,=
 which shall not be unreasonably withheld, conditioned or delayed.</div>
    <div>&nbsp;</div>
    <div>Section 2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <font s=
tyle=3D"font-weight: bold;"><u>Purchase Price</u>.</font></div>
    <div>&nbsp;</div>
    <div style=3D"text-align: justify; text-indent: 27pt;">(a)&nbsp;&nbsp;&=
nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The purchase price (the =93<=
u>Purchase Price</u>=94) to be paid by Buyer to Seller for the Property sha=
ll be Five Hundred Sixty Five Thousand Dollars ($565,000.00).</div>
    <div><br>
    </div>
    <div style=3D"text-indent: 27pt;"> (b)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nb=
sp;&nbsp;&nbsp; The Purchase Price shall be payable as follows:</div>
    <div> <br>
    </div>
    <div style=3D"text-align: justify; margin-left: 27pt; text-indent: 36pt=
;">(i)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; A deposit of Ten Tho=
usand Dollars ($10,000.00) shall be paid within three (3) business days aft=
er the Effective Date of this Agreement, by bank check (such payment is
      referred to herein as the =93<u>Deposit</u>=94).</div>
    <div><br>
    </div>
    <div style=3D"clear: both; margin-top: 10pt; margin-bottom: 10pt;" id=
=3D"DSPFPageBreakArea">
      <div id=3D"DSPFPageNumberArea" style=3D"text-align: center;"><font id=
=3D"DSPFPageNumber" style=3D"font-size: 8pt; font-weight: normal; font-styl=
e: normal;">1</font></div>
      <div style=3D"page-break-after:always;" id=3D"DSPFPageBreak">
        <hr noshade=3D"noshade" style=3D"margin: 4px 0px; width: 100%; bord=
er-width: 0; height: 2px; color: #000000; background-color: #000000; clear:=
 both;"></div>
    </div>
    <div style=3D"text-align: justify; margin-left: 27pt;">(ii)&nbsp;&nbsp;=
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; The balance of the Purchase Price, adj=
usted by apportionment as set forth herein, shall be paid at Closing (as de=
fined below) by bank cashier=92s check, certified check or attorney trust
      account check made payable to Seller, or by wire transfer pursuant to=
 written instructions given by Seller to Buyer prior to the Closing.</div>
    <div>&nbsp;</div>
    <div style=3D"text-align: justify;">Section 3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&=
nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <font style=3D"font-weight: bold;"><u>Deposit</u>.</font>=
<font style=3D"font-weight: bold;">&nbsp;</font>The Deposit shall be held b=
y MSK Attorneys (the =93<u>Escrow Agent</u>=94) in a non-interest bearing I=
OLTA
      trust account. The Deposit shall be applied to the Purchase Price at =
Closing. In the event the Closing does not occur, the Deposit shall be disb=
ursed as provided herein.</div>
    <div>&nbsp;</div>
    <div style=3D"text-align: justify;">Section 4.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp=
; &nbsp; <font style=3D"font-weight: bold;"><u>Buyer=92s Closing Conditions=
</u>.</font><font style=3D"font-weight: bold;">&nbsp;&nbsp; </font>Buyer=92=
s obligation to close shall be conditioned upon satisfaction of the
      following, in Buyer=92s discretion (the =93<u>Closing Conditions</u>=
=94):</div>
    <div>&nbsp;</div>
    <div>
      <div style=3D"text-align: justify; text-indent: 27pt;"><font style=3D=
"font-weight: normal;">(a)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; =
<u>Inspections</u>.</font><font style=3D"font-weight: normal;"> </font>Buye=
r=92s investigation, review and acceptance, in its sole discretion, of (i)
        the physical condition of the Property and the Building, including =
without limitation its compliance with fire and life safety codes and regul=
ations, and (ii) the environmental condition of the Property, all in accord=
ance with the following: Buyer
        and its engineers, inspectors, and other agents and representatives=
 (collectively, =93<u>Buyer=92s Agents</u>=94), and the Fire Marshal, are h=
ereby authorized to inspect the Property and conduct such reviews, tests an=
d studies and take such actions as
        Buyer shall deem appropriate in connection with its investigation o=
f the Property=92s physical and environmental condition.</div>
    </div>
    <div style=3D"text-indent: 27pt;">&nbsp;</div>
    <div style=3D"text-align: justify; text-indent: 27pt;">Buyer agrees tha=
t in conducting any inspections, investigations or tests, Buyer and Buyer=
=92s Agents shall: (i) not damage any part of the Property or any personal =
property owned or held by Seller;
      (ii) promptly pay when due the costs of all tests, investigations and=
 examinations done with regard to the Property; and (iii) not permit any li=
ens to attach to the Property by reason of the exercise of Buyer=92s rights=
 hereunder.</div>
    <div style=3D"text-indent: 27pt;">&nbsp;</div>
    <div style=3D"text-align: justify; text-indent: 27pt;">If any damage oc=
curs at the Property as a result of Buyer=92s due diligence activities, Buy=
er shall promptly restore the Property to the condition that existed prior =
to the commencement of the due
      diligence or such other activities, at Buyer=92s sole cost and expens=
e, and shall indemnify and save and hold Seller harmless from any claim, da=
mage, cost or expense, including reasonable attorneys=92 fees, for any phys=
ical damage to the Property arising
      from any inspections, tests, surveys and/or studies performed by Buye=
r or Buyer=92s Agents.</div>
    <div style=3D"text-indent: 27pt;">&nbsp;</div>
    <div style=3D"text-align: justify; text-indent: 27pt;">If the results o=
f Buyer=92s due diligence are not acceptable to Buyer, Buyer may, in Buyer=
=92s sole discretion, on or before the date that is forty-five (45) days af=
ter the Effective Date (the =93<u>Contingency</u><u>&nbsp;</u><u>Date</u>=
=94)


      elect to: (x) terminate this Agreement by providing written notice of=
 termination to Seller, in which case the Escrow Agent shall promptly disbu=
rse the Deposit to the Buyer and all of the rights and obligations of the p=
arties to this Agreement shall
      cease and terminate; or (y) waive the satisfaction of such Closing Co=
ndition and proceed with the purchase contemplated by this Agreement withou=
t a reduction in the Purchase Price, but subject, however, to the remaining=
 Closing Conditions set forth
      in this Agreement.</div>
    <div style=3D"text-indent: 27pt;">&nbsp;</div>
    <div style=3D"text-align: justify; text-indent: 27pt;">(b)&nbsp;&nbsp;&=
nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <u>Solar Facility Lease</u>. The partie=
s having agreed on the form of a lease to be executed at Closing with respe=
ct to Seller=92s post-Closing maintenance and operation of the Solar
      Facility from the roof of the Building (the =93<u>Solar Facility Leas=
e</u>=94).</div>
    <div style=3D"text-indent: 27pt;">&nbsp;</div>
    <div style=3D"text-align: justify; text-indent: 27pt;">(c)&nbsp; &nbsp;=
 &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp; <u>Representations and Warranties</u>. The representat=
ions and warranties made by the Seller in this Agreement being true and cor=
rect in all material respects on and as of the Closing
      with the same force and effect as though such representations and war=
ranties had been made as of the Closing.</div>
    <div>&nbsp;</div>
    <div style=3D"clear: both; margin-top: 10pt; margin-bottom: 10pt;" id=
=3D"DSPFPageBreakArea">
      <div id=3D"DSPFPageNumberArea" style=3D"text-align: center;"><font id=
=3D"DSPFPageNumber" style=3D"font-size: 8pt; font-weight: normal; font-styl=
e: normal;">2</font></div>
      <div style=3D"page-break-after:always;" id=3D"DSPFPageBreak">
        <hr noshade=3D"noshade" style=3D"margin: 4px 0px; width: 100%; bord=
er-width: 0; height: 2px; color: #000000; background-color: #000000; clear:=
 both;"></div>
    </div>
    <div style=3D"text-align: justify;">Section 5.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&=
nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <u><font style=3D"font-weight: bold;">Representations and=
</font><font style=3D"font-weight: bold;">&nbsp;</font><font style=3D"font-=
weight: bold;">Warranties of Seller</font></u><font style=3D"font-weight: b=
old;">.
      </font>Seller makes the following representations and warranties as o=
f the date of this Agreement and again as of the date of Closing:</div>
    <div><br>
    </div>
    <div style=3D"text-align: justify; text-indent: 27pt;">(a)&nbsp;&nbsp;&=
nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Seller is the record owner of the Prope=
rty and Buyer will be conveyed good, insurable, and marketable title to the=
 Property at Closing, free of all liens, tenants, occupants, and parties
      in possession, other than the Solar Facility Lease.</div>
    <div style=3D"text-indent: 27pt;">&nbsp;</div>
    <div style=3D"text-align: justify; text-indent: 27pt;">(b)&nbsp;&nbsp;&=
nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp; Seller has the full power and authority to e=
nter into, execute, deliver, and consummate the transaction contemplated by=
 this Agreement and any instruments and agreements contemplated
      herein. Seller has taken all action required by law to authorize the =
execution, delivery, and consummation of the transaction contemplated hereb=
y.</div>
    <div style=3D"text-indent: 27pt;">&nbsp;</div>
    <div style=3D"text-align: justify; text-indent: 27pt;">(c)&nbsp;&nbsp;&=
nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Seller warrants that the Pro=
perty is free from any unasserted mechanics' liens. At Closing, Seller shal=
l provide an affidavit attesting to the absence of claims of lien or potent=
ial lien
      owners, and further attesting that bills for improvements to the Prop=
erty made during the one hundred and eighty (180) days immediately precedin=
g the date of Closing have been paid in full.</div>
    <div style=3D"text-indent: 27pt;">&nbsp;</div>
    <div style=3D"text-align: justify; text-indent: 27pt;">(d)&nbsp;&nbsp;&=
nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Seller has not: (i) made a general assi=
gnment for the benefit of creditors; (ii) filed any voluntary petition in b=
ankruptcy or suffered the filing of an involuntary petition by its
      creditors; or (iii) suffered the appointment of a receiver to take po=
ssession of all or substantially all of its assets.</div>
    <div style=3D"text-indent: 27pt;">&nbsp;</div>
    <div style=3D"text-align: justify; text-indent: 27pt;">(e)&nbsp;&nbsp;&=
nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Seller has no knowledge of any li=
tigation or claim pending or threatened against it which would have an adve=
rse effect on the Property.</div>
    <div style=3D"text-indent: 27pt;">&nbsp;</div>
    <div style=3D"text-align: justify; text-indent: 27pt;">(f)&nbsp;&nbsp;&=
nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; There are no judgments, liens, actions,=
 encumbrances, or pending or threatened litigation against the Seller which=
 would have a material adverse effect on the use and operation of the
      Property or on the ability of Seller to consummate the transactions c=
ontemplated by this Agreement.</div>
    <div style=3D"text-indent: 27pt;">&nbsp;</div>
    <div style=3D"text-align: justify; text-indent: 27pt;">(g)&nbsp;&nbsp;&=
nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Seller is not a party to any contract, =
lease or other agreement or subject to any judgment, decree or order which =
materially and adversely affects the Property, or grants any third party
      the right to occupy all or any portion of the Property.</div>
    <div style=3D"text-indent: 27pt;">&nbsp;</div>
    <div style=3D"text-align: justify; text-indent: 27pt;">(h)&nbsp;&nbsp;&=
nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Seller has not received any notices fro=
m any insurance company of any defect in the Property which would materiall=
y affect the insurability of the Property.</div>
    <div style=3D"text-indent: 27pt;">&nbsp;</div>
    <div style=3D"text-align: justify; text-indent: 27pt;">(i)&nbsp;&nbsp;&=
nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;To the best of Seller=92s kn=
owledge, there is no existing latent structural or other physical defect in=
 the Property that materially impairs the current use or operation of the P=
roperty.</div>
    <div style=3D"text-indent: 27pt;">&nbsp;</div>
    <div style=3D"text-align: justify; text-indent: 27pt;">(j)&nbsp;&nbsp;&=
nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;To the best of Seller=92s kn=
owledge, (i) all permits, licenses, approvals and filings required by Gover=
nmental Regulations (defined below) for the Property have been obtained, an=
d the use,
      operation and condition of the Property does not violate any Governme=
ntal Regulations; and (ii) there are no unresolved civil, criminal or admin=
istrative action, suit, claim, hearing, investigation or proceeding has bee=
n brought or been threatened
      with respect to the Property=92s compliance with Governmental Regulat=
ions. =93<u>Governmental </u><u>Regulations</u>=94 means any local, state, =
or federal statute, ordinance, code, order, decree, law, rule or regulation=
 pertaining to or imposing liability
      or standards of conduct concerning land use and development.</div>
    <div style=3D"text-align: justify; text-indent: 27pt;"> <br>
    </div>
    <div style=3D"clear: both; margin-top: 10pt; margin-bottom: 10pt;" id=
=3D"DSPFPageBreakArea">
      <div id=3D"DSPFPageNumberArea" style=3D"text-align: center;"><font id=
=3D"DSPFPageNumber" style=3D"font-size: 8pt; font-weight: normal; font-styl=
e: normal;">3</font></div>
      <div style=3D"page-break-after:always;" id=3D"DSPFPageBreak">
        <hr noshade=3D"noshade" style=3D"margin: 4px 0px; width: 100%; bord=
er-width: 0; height: 2px; color: #000000; background-color: #000000; clear:=
 both;"></div>
    </div>
    <div style=3D"text-align: justify; text-indent: 27pt;">(k)&nbsp;&nbsp;&=
nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;To the best of Seller=92s kn=
owledge, there are no hazardous substances, hazardous wastes or regulated c=
ontaminants located on the Property, and no release of hazardous substances=
,
      hazardous wastes or regulated contaminants has occurred on, or has mi=
grated onto or beneath, the Property. As used herein, =93<u>Hazardous Subst=
ances</u>=94 means hazardous toxic substances, wastes, materials, pollutant=
s, contaminants, and any other
      similar substances or materials which are included under or regulated=
 by local, state, or federal law, rule, or regulation pertaining to protect=
ion of human health and the environment, or environmental contamination, cl=
ean-up, or disclosure,
      including the Comprehensive Environmental Response Compensation and L=
iability Action of 1980, 42 U.S.C. =A7 9601 <u>et</u> <u>seq.</u>, as amend=
ed (CERCLA), the Resource Conservation and Recovery Act of 1976, 42 U.S.C. =
=A7 9601 <u>et seq.</u>, as
      amended (RCRA), and the Vermont Waste Management Statutes, 10 V.S.A.,=
 Ch. 159, and regulations adopted pursuant to all such statutes.</div>
    <div><br>
    </div>
    <div style=3D"text-align: justify; text-indent: 27pt;">The warranties a=
nd representations contained in this Agreement shall not merge with the del=
ivery of deed to the Property and shall continue to remain in full force an=
d effect for a period of one year
      after the Closing. Buyer=92s remedy for a breach of the warranties ma=
de herein shall be an action in law or equity for such party=92s actual out=
-of-pocket damages, remedies, costs, penalties and expenses, including cour=
t costs and reasonable attorneys=92
      fees. The aggregate recovery of the Buyer with respect to the foregoi=
ng shall not exceed the Purchase Price.</div>
    <div><br>
    </div>
    <div style=3D"text-align: justify;">Section 6.&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbs=
p;&nbsp; <font style=3D"font-weight: bold;"><u>Closing</u>.</font></div>
    <div>&nbsp;</div>
    <div style=3D"text-align: justify; text-indent: 27pt;">(a)&nbsp;&nbsp;&=
nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The closing and transfer of =
title to the Property (the =93<u>Closing</u>=94) shall take place at the of=
fices of Buyer=92s counsel or lender, or via remote escrow closing, on the =
date that is
      forty-five (45) days after the Contingency Date (the =93<u>Closing Da=
te</u>=94), or at such other place or time as the parties may mutually agre=
e upon in writing. If the date that is forty-five (45) days after the Conti=
ngency Date is a holiday or
      weekend, then the Closing Date shall be extended to the second busine=
ss day thereafter.</div>
    <div style=3D"text-indent: 27pt;">&nbsp;</div>
    <div style=3D"text-align: justify; text-indent: 27pt;">(b)&nbsp;&nbsp;&=
nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; At Closing, possession and occupancy of=
 the Property shall be delivered to Buyer broom clean, and Seller shall lea=
ve the Property free from all tenants, occupants and parties in
      possession, other than the Solar Facility Lease.</div>
    <div style=3D"text-indent: 27pt;">&nbsp;</div>
    <div style=3D"text-align: justify; text-indent: 27pt;">(c)&nbsp;&nbsp;&=
nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Buyer shall have the right to phy=
sically inspect the Property at least three (3) days prior to Closing to en=
sure Seller=92s compliance with this provision.</div>
    <div>&nbsp;</div>
    <div style=3D"text-align: justify;">Section 7.&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;=
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <font style=3D"font-weight: bold;"><u>Transfer Documents=
.</u></font><font style=3D"font-weight: bold;">&nbsp; </font>At Closing, Se=
ller shall deliver to Buyer, against payment of the Purchase Price, in form
      satisfactory to Buyer and Buyer=92s counsel, the following (collectiv=
ely, the =93<u>Transfer Documents</u>=94):</div>
    <div>&nbsp;</div>
    <div style=3D"text-align: justify; text-indent: 27pt;">(a)&nbsp;&nbsp;&=
nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <u>Authority</u>. A resolution of Selle=
r, in recordable form, authorizing the transfer of the Property to Buyer an=
d appointing an individual to execute the Transfer Documents on behalf
      of Seller, together with evidence that Seller is a corporation duly o=
rganized and validly existing and in good standing under the laws of the St=
ate of Vermont.</div>
    <div style=3D"text-indent: 27pt;">&nbsp;</div>
    <div style=3D"text-align: justify; text-indent: 27pt;">(b)&nbsp;&nbsp;&=
nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <u>Warranty Deed</u>. A standard Vermon=
t Warranty Deed sufficient to convey to Buyer good, insurable, and marketab=
le title to the Property.</div>
    <div>&nbsp;</div>
    <div style=3D"clear: both; margin-top: 10pt; margin-bottom: 10pt;" id=
=3D"DSPFPageBreakArea">
      <div id=3D"DSPFPageNumberArea" style=3D"text-align: center;"><font id=
=3D"DSPFPageNumber" style=3D"font-size: 8pt; font-weight: normal; font-styl=
e: normal;">4</font></div>
      <div style=3D"page-break-after:always;" id=3D"DSPFPageBreak">
        <hr noshade=3D"noshade" style=3D"margin: 4px 0px; width: 100%; bord=
er-width: 0; height: 2px; color: #000000; background-color: #000000; clear:=
 both;"></div>
    </div>
    <div style=3D"text-indent: 27pt;">(c)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbs=
p;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <u>Transfer Tax Return</u>. A completed Vermont Proper=
ty Transfer Tax Return.</div>
    <div><br>
    </div>
